WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.391 --> 00:00:02.570
- Your name is so unique, it's Madelaine.

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:03.980
- Madelaine, yeah.
- Madelaine!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.813
Oh, really!

00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:06.230
- But my parents are hippies, and my--

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.063
- [Kelly] Love it!

00:00:07.063 --> 00:00:09.070
- Very hippies, we would
eat from the garden,

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.940
my parents are vegans,
very crazy little kookies.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.853
But my dad wanted to name me Street.

00:00:13.853 --> 00:00:14.880
- Street!
- Which,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.620
if we can just imagine for a second,

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.990
a poor little six-year-old
in elementary school,

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.760
like, "Gonna go walk
down the 'Street' today,"

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.270
people would make so many jokes about it.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.486
- Yeah, well, I named my kid River.

00:00:24.486 --> 00:00:26.499
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:27.332
- Whoops!
- So I don't know that

00:00:27.332 --> 00:00:28.260
that's any better.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.330
- So, my mom was like,
"No, we have to do Lane,"

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.340
like, lane on the road, Madelaine, street.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.130
So that was like a compromise, you know?

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.010
- I love your name, though,
I think it separates you out!

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.810
I think Madeline, Madeline
is beautiful enough,

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.370
but Madelaine is, it's gorgeous!

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.203
- Thank you so much!

00:00:40.203 --> 00:00:41.112
So is Kelly!
- Well done, hippies!

00:00:41.112 --> 00:00:42.030
- And Rob, look at that.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.234
- Well done, possibly a lot of pot!

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:44.201
(audience applauds)
(Madelaine laughing)

00:00:44.201 --> 00:00:45.260
Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.800
Well done!

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.870
So, you had a lot of odd jobs, here in LA.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.244
I did as well, when I moved
here after high school, so--

00:00:50.244 --> 00:00:51.077
- You did?

00:00:51.077 --> 00:00:51.910
I'm fascinated.
- Yes.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:52.960
What were yours?
- I want to ask you,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.730
but okay, you can ask me first.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.790
Six years ago, I would go
knock on people's doors,

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.300
and try to sell them new windows.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.210
- Oh! Yeah.
- But I did it for two hours.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.219
- Why wouldn't you knock on their windows?

00:01:01.219 --> 00:01:02.753
- Why? (laughing)
(audience laughs)

00:01:02.753 --> 00:01:03.586
- Should I break the window?

00:01:03.586 --> 00:01:05.040
- [Kelly] Because that seems creepy.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.507
- I should have broken the
window and then be like,

00:01:06.507 --> 00:01:07.930
"Looks like you need a new window!"

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:08.990
(audience laughs)
(Kelly claps)

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.080
I woulda made some money then.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.990
- That's amazing!
- Yeah, that was a weird job.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.184
- I was a projectionist
at the Malibu Cinema,

00:01:14.184 --> 00:01:15.600
when I was 13.
- Oh my God, my first job

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.450
was a movie theater!
- What?

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.750
Wait, when you were 13 years old?

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.323
- Yeah, it was truly child labor.

00:01:19.323 --> 00:01:20.646
- Yeah, honestly!
- Like, violations.

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:23.380
(audience laughs)
But I put the reels on

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.390
in the wrong order.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.407
- [Kelly] Oh, we--

00:01:25.407 --> 00:01:26.260
(Madelaine laughs)
- Like, my job was to

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.770
literally thread the projector.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.980
- But man, you screw that up,
you definitely ruin the film.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:30.815
- It was over, yep.
- [Kelly] Like, "You know,

00:01:30.815 --> 00:01:31.648
Bruce Willis dies."
- That was the end

00:01:31.648 --> 00:01:32.481
of my career as a projectionist.

00:01:32.481 --> 00:01:33.460
- [Kelly] In 'The Sixth Sense.'"

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.293
- So I was like, "You know what?

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.880
"Maybe I'll just be in movies."

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.713
- That's how you decided?

00:01:36.713 --> 00:01:38.435
- It was a better trade, I feel.

00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:39.273
(audience applauds)
- Yes!

